Versions are milestones, not calendar releases, and the third number is
the point release: it increments when a verified deliverable lands inside
the current milestone. Each entry names the gate that verified it. See
doc/README.roadmap.md for the exit criteria of each milestone.

Nothing here is released. No tag exists, and the driver does not mount.

v0.1.10
=======
- Reader-facing documents audited against the tree: three gates named in
  no document or CI step, a control claim that was false for four of six
  gates, an errno count that had never matched its baseline, two drifted
  line counts, a CI comment naming the wrong kernel floor
- Origin table's line counts now derived rather than maintained by hand
- Verified by: script/test-inventory.sh, falsified on a perturbed doc, a
  perturbed file, and a non-numeric count column

v0.1.9
======
- Citation gate anchors on the whole backticked token rather than its
  first identifier, so a row anchored on a common word is reported as
  weak instead of counted as a pass
- Verified by: script/test-citations.sh, which now grades each pass by
  anchor strength

v0.1.8
======
- The 0.1.x rows audited against the tree rather than against the table,
  and the one overclaim corrected: README.status.md had put inode and
  subr in the carried set on no cited authority
- Verified by: script/test-citations.sh, falsified one invocation at a
  time on a one-line drift, a citation to a file that does not exist, a
  line past end of file, and an emptied population

v0.1.7
======
- Gate over the three hand-maintained lists that claim to cover
  src/sys/fs/hammer2: the origin table, the Makefile's hammer2-y, and
  the filenames script/test-syntax.sh names one by one
- Verified by: script/test-inventory.sh, falsified with a planted .c
  that produces one finding per list; population asserted

v0.1.6
======
- The roadmap's history table got a gate
- The module's absent MODULE_LICENSE recorded with what decides its value
- Style gate stopped writing a baseline and exiting 0 when it found none
- Verified by: script/test-history.sh, falsified on an unresolvable hash
  and on a table whose rows stop matching

v0.1.5
======
- The 64 KiB inventory: thirteen sites, seven belonging to the on-disk
  format and six to the folio decision, in doc/IO_MODEL.md
- Verified by: the inventory itself, each site cited to a line

v0.1.4
======
- Vendored sys/tree.h and sys/queue.h stopped redefining the kernel's
  LIST_HEAD and RB_ROOT
- Verified by: script/test-syntax.sh, extended to gcc beside clang under
  a W=1 warning set; both compilers reported the redefinitions
  independently, which is what made them credible rather than stylistic

v0.1.3
======
- The folio ceiling's design recorded: a mount-time capability check by
  name, mapping_max_folio_size_supported(), with the build-time
  transparent hugepage assert kept as the bootstrap instrument until a
  mount path exists
- Verified by: doc/README.porting.md, The DIO layer

v0.1.2
======
- Kernel version floor corrected from memory to measurement: 6.15, set by
  BLK_MAX_BLOCK_SIZE, with each symbol dated at the tag where it appeared
- Verified by: the table in doc/README.status.md, and an #error in
  hammer2_os.h that matches it

v0.1.1
======
- Style gate's sort made locale-independent, after a first CI run failed
  with every count identical and four lines in a different order
- Verified by: script/test-checkpatch.sh byte-comparing its baseline

v0.1.0
======
- Initial import
- OS shim (hammer2_os.h, hammer2_compat.h)
- DIO layer on the block device page cache
- On-disk format, ioctl and in-memory headers
- Vendored sys/tree.h and sys/queue.h
- Verified by: script/test-shim.sh, script/test-syntax.sh
